# Python rules

> Applies to: `src/**/*.py`, `tests/**/*.py`
> Toolchain version: Python 3.12  ·  Package manager: uv

## Commands (run from repo root)

| Purpose        | Command                                   |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Install deps   | `uv sync`                                  |
| Build          | N/A                                        |
| Run (dev)      | `uv run python -m app`                     |
| Test (all)     | `uv run pytest`                            |
| Test (single)  | `uv run pytest tests/test_x.py::test_case` |
| Lint           | `uv run ruff check .`                      |
| Format         | `uv run ruff format .`                     |
| Typecheck      | `uv run mypy src`                          |

- `ruff format` is **authoritative** — don't hand-format; run it.
- Before declaring done: run format, lint, typecheck, and tests (see root DoD).

## Style & structure

- Config lives in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.ruff]`, `[tool.mypy]`) — don't override inline unless noted there.
- Naming: `snake_case` functions/vars, `PascalCase` classes, `UPPER_SNAKE` constants.
- Layout: one cohesive concern per module; keep files < 300 LOC per root rule.
- Public functions/classes get docstrings; comments explain *why*, not *what*.
- Prefer type hints everywhere; mypy runs in strict-ish mode.

## Errors & logging

- Raise specific exceptions; never `except:` bare or empty (matches root no-empty-try/catch rule). Fail fast — no silent fallbacks.
- Use the `logging` module, not `print`, in committed code. Never log secrets or PII.

## Testing

- pytest; tests live in `tests/` mirroring `src/`.
- New code ships with tests. Don't skip/`xfail` to make a suite green.
- Unit-test logic in isolation; use fixtures for I/O boundaries.

## Dependencies

- Add via `uv add <pkg>`; commit `uv.lock`.
- Pin versions via the lockfile; prefer maintained, permissively licensed libs.
- Qualify a new dependency with the user before adding it (root rule).
- Do not hand-edit generated/vendored files: `uv.lock`, migrations, `*_pb2.py`.

## Language-specific gotchas

- Async: don't mix blocking I/O into `async def`; use `asyncio`-aware libs.
- Mutable default args are forbidden (`def f(x=[])`) — use `None` sentinels.
